# AI Pipeline Rules

## Structured output
- Always Vercel AI SDK `generateObject` with a Zod schema.
- `generateText + JSON.parse` is forbidden — schemas are the contract.
- Schemas live colocated with the service that uses them, exported as `const X = z.object(...)` plus `export type X = z.infer<typeof X>`.
- Every Zod field gets a `.describe()` — the LLM reads these as field hints.

## LLM calls
- Go through `LlmService.understandQuery(...)`, `LlmService.summarizeDelta(...)`, etc. Never call `generateObject` directly outside `LlmService`.
- All LlmService public methods wrap generation in `this.withFreeTierFallback(...)` for 429 backoff + cascade.
- Free-model cascade comes from `getFreeModelCascade()` in `src/config/env.ts`. Don't hard-code model names anywhere.

## Delta detection (cheapest first)
1. Numeric rules — for tracked numbers (prices, rates), compare snapshot N vs N-1.
2. Embedding cosine — pgvector similarity to last 5 snapshots → novelty score.
3. LLM verdict — only when (1) and (2) are inconclusive.

Document the threshold per stage in code comments.

## Embeddings
- Use `EmbeddingsService` only. Never call `@xenova/transformers` directly elsewhere.
- 384-dim `Xenova/bge-small-en-v1.5`. If the column dimension changes, version the column and write a backfill.
- Warm the pipeline at NestJS bootstrap (`onModuleInit`) so first-request latency stays low.

## Cost & rate limits
- Use the smallest free model that does the job — DeepSeek V3 free is the default for everything BriefIQ needs.
- Free tier: 20 RPM / 200 RPD unfunded, 1000 RPD funded.
- Backoff on 429: handled by `withFreeTierFallback`. Don't reinvent it.

## Prompt hygiene
- Prompts are `const SYSTEM_PROMPT = \`...\`` at the top of the service file (before any `@Injectable`).
- Reference the Zod schema by intent in the prompt; don't list every field by name.
- Include 1 worked example per prompt for tasks where output quality is fragile.

## Memory & dedup
- Before generating a briefing, check pgvector cosine vs last 30 days of briefings for the user.
- If similarity > 0.92 → skip (already told them).

## Adding a new prompt
- Follow [.cursor/skills/add-llm-prompt/SKILL.md](../skills/add-llm-prompt/SKILL.md) end-to-end.
